{"results":[{"url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2020/10/29/azerbaijan-mcdonalds-nagorno-karabakh/","final_url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2020/10/29/azerbaijan-mcdonalds-nagorno-karabakh/","title":"In the fight between Armenia and Azerbaijan, even a McDonald’s is taking sides","description":"After military clashes between Azerbaijan and Armenia broke out last month, fast-food franchisees began to weigh in — on behalf of Azerbaijan.","language":"en","text":"In the fight between Armenia and Azerbaijan, even a McDonald’s is taking sides\n\nDuring the last week of September, renewed fighting between Armenia and Azerbaijan began, causing concerns of a possible broader escalation. (Video: Alexa Juliana Ard, Rick Noack/The Washington Post)\n\nIn Azerbaijan, as elsewhere, McDonald’s and Burger King stores tend to use their Instagram accounts to post photos of burgers and fries. But a few weeks ago, the tone took a turn.\n\nAfter military clashes between Azerbaijan and Armenia broke out last month, fast-food franchisees began to weigh in — on behalf of Azerbaijan.","author":"Rick Noack","published_date":"2020-10-30T16:58:06.851Z","latency_ms":1635.8421100012492,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}